/-
# Sparse groups with undecidable word problem (Kourovka Notebook Problem 7.24)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 7.24 (A. V. Kuznetsov): we say that a group
is sparse if the variety generated by it has at most countably many subvarieties. Does there exist a
finitely generated sparse group that has undecidable word problem?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentClassFourVarietyLatticeKourovka3Problem53Wanted
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.WordProblemSolvableShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SparseGroupUndecidableWordProblemKourovka7Problem24Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 7.24 (A. V.
Kuznetsov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700423 (`KOU-7.24`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Varieties are described by their laws in the free group `FreeGroup ℕ` of countable rank: the
subvarieties of the variety generated by `G` correspond bijectively to the fully invariant subgroups
(`IsFullyInvariant` of Kourovka 3.53) containing the laws of `G`, so
`G` is sparse when there are countably many of those. Undecidable word problem is the negation of
`WordProblemSolvable` (`WantedExt/GroupTheory/WordProblemSolvableShared.lean`) for a surjection
`FreeGroup (Fin n) →* G`, i.e. for a finite generating tuple (solvability does not depend on the
tuple).
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentClassFourVarietyLatticeKourovka3Problem53Wanted
  (IsFullyInvariant)
open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.WordProblemSolvableShared

/-- The laws of `G`: the words of the free group `FreeGroup ℕ` of countable rank that vanish under
every homomorphism `FreeGroup ℕ →* G`. -/
def lawSubgroup (G : Type) [Group G] : Subgroup (FreeGroup ℕ) :=
  ⨅ f : FreeGroup ℕ →* G, f.ker

/-- `G` is sparse (A. V. Kuznetsov): the variety generated by `G` has at most countably many
subvarieties. The subvarieties correspond to the fully invariant subgroups of `FreeGroup ℕ` (their
sets of laws) that contain the laws of `G`. -/
def IsSparse (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  {V : Subgroup (FreeGroup ℕ) | IsFullyInvariant V ∧ lawSubgroup G ≤ V}.Countable

/-- Kourovka 7.24 (A. V. Kuznetsov): there is a finitely generated sparse group with undecidable
word problem. -/
def sparseGroupUndecidableWordProblem : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G) (n : ℕ) (φ : FreeGroup (Fin n) →* G),
    Function.Surjective φ ∧ IsSparse G ∧ ¬ WordProblemSolvable φ

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 7.24 "Yes, such groups do exist", giving a free group of
the variety `N₃A` (nilpotent of class at most `3` by abelian) as an example: every subvariety of
`N₃A` is finitely based by Krasil'nikov (1991), so there are only countably many, and the word
problem is undecidable by Kharlampovich (1988). Kharlampovich's paper (zbMATH Zbl 0662.17003) proves
that every group variety containing `ZN₂A ⊆ N₃A` has a finitely presented group with unsolvable word
problem; such a group in `N₃A` is also a finitely generated sparse group with undecidable word
problem. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The
Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 7.24
(A. V. Kuznetsov); resolution: A. N. Krasil'nikov, The identities of a group with nilpotent
commutator subgroup are finitely based, Math. USSR-Izv. 37 (1991), 539-553; O. G. Kharlampovich, The
equality problem in the variety ZN₂A, Sov. Math. 32, no. 11 (1988), 136-140, Kourovka Archive,
Problem 7.24: Yes, such groups do exist, for example a free group of N₃A: every subvariety of N₃A is
finitely based (Krasil'nikov), hence there are only countably many, and its word problem is
undecidable (Kharlampovich), https://doi.org/10.1070/IM1991v037n03ABEH002158.
-/
public theorem_wanted sparseGroupUndecidableWordProblem_holds : sparseGroupUndecidableWordProblem

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SparseGroupUndecidableWordProblemKourovka7Problem24Wanted
